  "body": "Direct-PR: operator-requested fix of `hygiene.py` (confirmed to the steward in session 2026-11-05), tooling only, self-merged when CI is green.\n\nThe problem: a blocked lot whose lot dependencies are all done but whose capture issue is still open was skipped in silence, so the stale blocks on LOT-089 #181, LOT-102 #193 and LOT-136 #226 were never surfaced.\n\nThe cause: the sweep skips every capture-gated lot before reporting.\n\nWhat changed: one extra report line listing those lots with their open captures (never an unblock: the capture decides), plus one line in `tooling/roadmap/README.md`.\n\nTests: `test_blocked_lot_with_every_dependency_done_but_a_capture_open_is_reported` (fails without the change, passes with it); the 32 roadmap tests pass.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CEBkjmFApUaMrewUvD)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Roadmap reports now identify blocked items whose dependencies are complete but that remain gated by an open capture. The report includes the affected item and capture, and these items remain blocked rather than being treated as ready for automatic unblocking.\n* **Documentation**\n  * Updated the roadmap hygiene description to reflect reporting for items gated by an open capture.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
