   "body": "<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n<a href=\"https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/456?scope=ghh_OusAJGA4HG8ljoOV0wJvVx8NmnZIjc2DdjmxOu0xZWA&amp;cs_source=review_comment\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-buttons-v1/explain-change-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-buttons-v1/explain-change.svg\"><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-buttons-v1/explain-change.svg\" alt=\"Explain Change →\" height=\"32\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: failure by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> ## Review failed\n> \n> The pull request is closed.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: failure by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Walkthrough</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<br>\n\nThe roadmap hygiene analysis now reports blocked lots whose dependencies are done but that remain gated by an open capture. A test checks this report, and the README describes the added case.\n\n**Changes: Capture-gated lot reporting**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|:---|:---|\n|**Capture-gated lot detection and reporting** <br> `tooling/roadmap/hygiene.py`, `scripts/tests/test_roadmap.py`, `tooling/roadmap/README.md`|The analysis reports eligible blocked lots whose dependencies have no open or unknown items and whose identified gate is an open capture. The test checks that the lot and capture appear in the report, and the README describes the report case.|\n\n<!-- change_assessment_start -->\n**Estimated code review effort:** 2 (Simple) | ~8 minutes\n\n<!-- change_assessment_commit:\"a98a252fa39238ea05c4af68c355e428c85272ca\" -->\n**Change:** Bug fix\n<!-- change_assessment_end -->\n\n**Possibly related issues**\n- `ezzz/HFRnow#337`: The issue describes open captures that block lots; the new report identifies lots gated by open captures.\n- `ezzz/HFRnow#56`: LOT-028 has completed dependencies and is gated by capture `#133`, matching the reported state.\n- `ezzz/HFRnow#324`: The roadmap board lists lots waiting on captures, which the new report identifies.\n\n**Possibly related PRs**\n- [ezzz/HFRnow#370](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/370): This PR adds the hygiene analysis and capture data that the current change uses.\n- [ezzz/HFRnow#376](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/376): Its capture-blocker definition affects the capture set used by the new report.\n- [ezzz/HFRnow#433](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/433): The current report uses the M5 classification added by this PR.\n\n**Suggested labels:** `direct-pr`\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Merge Risk:</strong> <strong><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/risk-low-16.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture> Low</strong> · up to <code>a98a2</code></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<br>\n\n<!-- final_review_risk_start -->\n<!-- final_review_risk_label\n**Merge Risk:** **🔵 Low** · up to `a98a2`\n-->\n<!-- final_review_risk_coverage:{\"sourceCommitId\":\"a98a252fa39238ea05c4af68c355e428c85272ca\",\"coveredCommitId\":\"a98a252fa39238ea05c4af68c355e428c85272ca\",\"kind\":\"reviewed\"} -->\n\nThe hygiene report can misrepresent why lots remain blocked, reducing roadmap triage accuracy. The fixes are localized and the change does not automatically unblock these lots.\n<!-- final_review_risk_end -->\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n<!-- autopilot:start -->\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\"} --> <strong title=\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\">Autofix</strong> · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\n<!-- autopilot:end -->",
